{"content":[{"c":["ARPAD"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City in northern Syria. Arpad was overrun twice by the Assyrians: in 740 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," by Tiglath-pileser III and in 720 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," by Sargon II. The Assyrians used Arpad and Hamath as examples of the inability of any gods, including Israel’s, to protect cities against Assyria’s attacks (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.18.34","r":"2Kgs.18.34","rawR":"2Kgs.18.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.18.34","value":"2Kgs.18.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 18:34"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.19.13","r":"2Kgs.19.13","rawR":"2Kgs.19.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.19.13","value":"2Kgs.19.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.10.9","r":"Isa.10.9","rawR":"Isa.10.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.10.9","value":"Isa.10.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 10:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.36.19","r":"Isa.36.19","rawR":"Isa.36.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.36.19","value":"Isa.36.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"36:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.37.13","r":"Isa.37.13","rawR":"Isa.37.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.37.13","value":"Isa.37.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"37:13"},"). Arpad and Hamath are also mentioned in a later prophecy against the Syrian city of Damascus (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.49.23","r":"Jer.49.23","rawR":"Jer.49.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.49.23","value":"Jer.49.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 49:23"},"). Arpad has been identified as modern Tell Erfad, north of Aleppo."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Arpad","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 18:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.18.34","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.18.34","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.18.34"},{"anchorText":"19:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.19.13","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.19.13","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.19.13"},{"anchorText":"Is 10:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.10.9","rawQueryValue":"Isa.10.9","sourceRefExact":"Isa.10.9"},{"anchorText":"36:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.36.19","rawQueryValue":"Isa.36.19","sourceRefExact":"Isa.36.19"},{"anchorText":"37:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.37.13","rawQueryValue":"Isa.37.13","sourceRefExact":"Isa.37.13"},{"anchorText":"Jer 49:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.49.23","rawQueryValue":"Jer.49.23","sourceRefExact":"Jer.49.23"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b2770896a3055f497dde7e0604322abcadba17a9f718854b90969fefd8a1696d","sourceItemName":"Arpad","sourceItemOrder":503,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Arpad","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Arpad","title":"Arpad","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}